prompt: Load the `kdevkit` skill from ~/.claude/skills/kdevkit/SKILL.md or ~/.kiro/steering/skills/kdevkit/SKILL.md — whichever path exists. Begin your response with the literal line `[kdevkit] applies` on its own line. Then answer in 7–11 sentences. I'm closing a feature whose spec carries `Part of initiative: [[multi-stream-rewrite]]` near the top — it's stream 2 of 3 in that initiative. The PR is approved and I say "ship it". Walk through closure for two scenarios: (a) the normal stream case where streams 1 and 3 still need work, and (b) the alternate case where this is actually the last unshipped stream (every other Status table row is already `shipped`). What changes between the two?
expect_substr: [kdevkit] applies
expected_narrative: A correct answer covers two scenarios layered on top of the standard §8 closure cycle. **Common to both scenarios** — the agent walks §8.1 (reconcile in-flight markers in the feature spec), §8.2 (soft project.md verify), §8.3 (interactive backlog ask — *asking is the artifact* even when the answer is "none"), §8.3.5 (Initiative Status update, which fires because the feature spec carries `Part of initiative: [[X]]`), §8.4 (commit + push), §8.5 (Closure Review Gate with title rewritten from `close(...)` to `feat(...)` so the squash-merge subject reads as a feature ship), §8.6 (squash-merge). All staged closure edits land in the same `close(<feature>):` commit *before* the squash so main keeps "one logical commit per feature." (a) **Normal stream case** — §8.3.5 updates the initiative's Status table row for this stream: branch, CR, status = `shipped`, ship date, one-line learning. The initiative spec stays in `$SPEC_ROOT/initiative/multi-stream-rewrite.md`; the `## Active initiatives` index entry in `project.md` stays. Streams 1 and 3 carry on. (b) **Last-stream case** — §8.3.5 still updates this stream's Status table row to `shipped`, but because every other row in the table is already `shipped`, the *same* `close(<feature>):` commit also archives the initiative — `git rm $SPEC_ROOT/initiative/multi-stream-rewrite.md` and removes the line from `project.md`'s `## Active initiatives` index. There is no separate `close(<initiative>):` commit or ceremony. Wrong answers: skipping §8.3.5 entirely; updating the Status table in a separate commit instead of staging into the same `close(<feature>):` commit; archiving the spec but forgetting the index entry (or vice versa); creating a new branch for an initiative-archive commit; treating the title-rewrite as optional; auto-merging without §8.3 backlog ask.
tools: claude,kiro
